#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1260.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199261} :activity/id #uuid "a0472270-5f40-5310-8129-ab5eb91d56d0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048585 :topic/id #uuid "abbe9530-902a-5d99-8c65-74734dada530" :topic/math-academy-id 4173} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199261 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199457 :tutorial/content "Recall that the moments of inertia $I_x$ and $I_y$ of a thin plate $D$ about the $x$- and $y$- axes are given by\n\n$$\nI_x = \\iint\\limits_D y^2\\,\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm dA \\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\nI_y = \\iint\\limits_D x^2\\,\\lambda(x,y) \\:\\textrm dA,\n$$\n\nwhere the factors $y^2$ and $x^2$ represent the squared distances from a point on the plate to the $x$- and $y$-axes, respectively.\n\nIn general, the **moment of inertia about an axis $l$** of a plane lamina occupying the region $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda(x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the point $(x,y)$ to the axis $l.$\n\nFor example, consider the thin plate that occupies the region\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -1 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwith mass density function $\\lambda(x,y) = 3x+6.$ Let's find its moment of inertia about the line $y=2.$\n\n![](images/24/2451a992f9ecdea8aa1775b64b3a182e0df3f7eab8cac87307c49ed164c6b813.png)\n\nThe distance between a point $(x,y)$ on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |2 - y|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(3x+6)\\,|2-y{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}3(x+2)(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+2)\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}3(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{2}]}_{-1}^{1}\\cdot [(y-2)^{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-1+8) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "a69630f6-6774-5350-b275-26cd501135dc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5070 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "a7b5aafb-1437-5b53-ac08-026c4b750ce9" :step/math-academy-id 31760 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199342}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199342 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198415 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198057 :question/id #uuid "985e1b18-0023-55ba-b4e4-69a109d8de58" :question/math-academy-id "e-12485"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049331} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050409}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198644} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198646} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235555} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281669} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281671} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281674} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281675} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281679} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372223} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429803} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429804}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"} :step/id #uuid "30041ef5-a8d3-542d-8b3b-ca183a630d86" :step/math-academy-id 44957 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199343}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199343 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198416 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198058 :question/id #uuid "eab955a5-019b-5219-b5d5-32e3818be4b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-12486"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198647} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198648} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284384} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284385} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284386} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284387} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372230} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372237} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429800} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429801} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445636}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"} :step/id #uuid "c09c8fe7-04df-57bb-b640-89d79bf7712b" :step/math-academy-id 44958 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199345}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199345 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198418 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198060 :question/id #uuid "0f7dbe9f-b448-5e76-9932-68e1ff99904e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12488"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4820138b-483c-5ced-8df9-9849f5f2a7cb" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198649} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198650} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284395} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284398} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284399} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284416} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372244} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372251} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429802} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445635} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445637}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia Given a Description of a Mass Density Function"} :step/id #uuid "002ea8cc-7e94-5a8f-b910-6fbfdf671dcd" :step/math-academy-id 44962}] :activity/title "Moments of Inertia of Laminas About Other Axes" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186198499}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445640} :activity/id #uuid "eb4e0c90-e4bf-5334-a41e-c9dcbc6b2de0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048585 :topic/id #uuid "abbe9530-902a-5d99-8c65-74734dada530" :topic/math-academy-id 4173} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445638 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198647 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98e4d481-4d0b-5991-947a-60a55fac4b94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14M}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194514} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a52d32-d438-5888-b585-de23d106a91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194515} {:answer/id #uuid "25108cf6-a5d4-5591-9e26-2fa461336e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194516} {:answer/id #uuid "33601e3a-9efe-53c8-8251-715c3ff6c2b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194517} {:answer/id #uuid "58026407-822b-5ddb-bc51-52cc7ca66ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194518}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186194517} :answer-field/id #uuid "255e3447-a66a-534b-a9be-bd3d61fb7682" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194513}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "56c1de07-70ce-5967-9f10-9a87cc16b398" :question/math-academy-id "q-162998" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,3\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 1=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}({\\int }_{3}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot [x]_{3}^{5}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y-2)^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(5-3)(\\frac{1}{3}(1-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(0-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =M(-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "07466f53-e252-509d-8a34-a405145acef5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445641}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445639 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445635 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b7a4ed-6a62-5958-af18-fb40a86462b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{6M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445617} {:answer/id #uuid "6abdd6fd-84fe-5787-9074-401ecc94520e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{29M}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445619} {:answer/id #uuid "c76013eb-2e60-5dc8-b1fd-86c086d4bcfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{128M}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445625} {:answer/id #uuid "ce166fcb-1dfc-519c-a85d-161ea72636a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445627} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2a98ac-fbb8-5412-baa1-04362a35b51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15M}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445631}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445627} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5556ed2-662d-582b-a0da-d02820904882" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3a407e50-1493-5ac2-abfc-afeed102785c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163652" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}(8-0)(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=\\frac{3M}{8}{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{8}{x}^{2}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{8}{x}^{2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}({\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}-{x}^{4}+\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[y]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}\\cdot (\\frac{32}{5}-16+\\frac{32}{3})\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}\\cdot \\frac{16}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "75f7502b-d79d-5e16-8da0-486fac5f9f4b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445642}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445640 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198646 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9837ac6e-33c5-557e-bb9e-fe958115ad42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194508} {:answer/id #uuid "a3307aef-e8c9-57f5-82b9-ab274cd1f1b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194509} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d7cc8f-90c8-5f4f-b57b-48dc41dc82d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194510} {:answer/id #uuid "24fb16b8-6d77-5edd-99d8-2ae286c4a79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194511} {:answer/id #uuid "37791a65-7718-530f-ac49-2acec54f930e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194512}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186194510} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b189c65-1537-5ff7-ab90-0c5ea8921d6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "baa9befe-f934-5d8a-99b8-4dbfdbb636a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162993" :question/problem "![](images/df/df0ffdd8bfb94ece82926411bfddb3affc85e802807a36cb2e8ee9b9b727633c.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $x$-axis and the lines $y=x$ and $y=2-x$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=3x+2.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,y\\le x\\le 2-y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/d1/d1241b56d482f24cc06d51a9aaecbc623805df0a76739201e5cbe6974e2e9c6f.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-1|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}(3x+2)|y-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}(3x+2)(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)[{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}3x+2\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1){[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+2x]}_{x=y}^{x=2-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)[\\frac{3}{2}(2-y)^{2}+2(2-y)-(\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2y)]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =10{\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)(1-y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =10{\\int }_{0}^{1}1-3y+3{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =10{[y-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =10(1-\\frac{3}{2}+1-\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "af1f1335-4b99-5b58-9b75-fe6f46cf00ad" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445638}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445641 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7faf4b7f-4f51-54e5-8676-2aff35a9aba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445620} {:answer/id #uuid "b4815fe0-0696-5b13-b4e7-7c49e55ee3fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445622} {:answer/id #uuid "c351d508-c06d-56b5-81fc-74bc138267ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445624} {:answer/id #uuid "dfeaebde-f303-5342-a31a-0aa1900de703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445629} {:answer/id #uuid "e4cb05b1-5665-5f7f-bb6c-6b8055b9e402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445630}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445620} :answer-field/id #uuid "845cdc46-a35a-5586-a626-09720ae6b110" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5254f44e-1aee-5d92-b378-2e98dcb05199" :question/math-academy-id "q-163619" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=-2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y+2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}|y+2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}(y+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{-1}^{1}(y+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot [x]_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y+2)^{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(2-1)(\\frac{1}{3}(1+2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(-1+2)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(9-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{13M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bf1ba95f-9b2b-5cae-8cac-39eec0a7a2c4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445639}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445642 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445637 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f3cd980-48ea-571b-9b45-60baf14b36fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445618} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4ed41d-46b1-5cfa-ac2b-42be83590f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445621} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f6f1aa-4c77-51d1-8803-77e7ade1835f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445623} {:answer/id #uuid "c82691e9-9f25-55f2-9f79-61a4e0f60f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "13M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445626} {:answer/id #uuid "d4bef6bd-0aec-5f69-bb41-4ec8057c0acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445628}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445626} :answer-field/id #uuid "641b9e4b-4711-52d7-948a-1033dbe4f079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bff66772-3aa9-52e4-ae38-3aff93ff5b7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163664" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le 0,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{3}k{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot [x]_{-3}^{0}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}(0-(-3))(27-1) \\\\  & =26k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2}=\\frac{M}{26}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{M}{26}{y}^{2}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{M}{26}{y}^{2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}({\\int }_{-3}^{0}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}\\cdot {[\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{3}]}_{-3}^{0}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}\\cdot (-\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{125}{3})\\cdot (9-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}\\cdot 39\\cdot \\frac{26}{3} \\\\  & =13M.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f0e756d4-4310-5dd8-bca5-e3e7d601cc8a"}] :activity/title "Moments of Inertia of Laminas About Other Axes" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445616}]}
